.* WRKJRN: the journals a name selects, with the recovery options.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=JRN CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JRNLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ASPDEV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JRNTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=JRNS VARS='OPT JRN JRNLIB ASPDEV JRNTEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=WJKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKJRN KEYL=WJKEYS HELP=WRKJRN ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Journals
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JRNS.(No journals match specified name)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?APYJRNCHG JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.2=Forward recovery
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD ?RMVJRNCHG JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.3=Backout recovery
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJRNA JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.5=Display journal status
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='RETURN 6'.6=Recover damaged journal
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ENTER='RETURN 7'.7=Recover damaged journal receivers
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJRNA JRN(&JRNLIB./&JRN.)'.8=Work with journal attributes
:LISTACT OPTION=9 ENTER='RETURN 9'.9=Associate receivers with journal
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=JRN USAGE=OUTPUT.Journal
:LISTCOL VAR=JRNLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:LISTGRP COL=ASPGRP.ASP
:LISTCOL VAR=ASPDEV USAGE=OUTPUT.Device
:ELISTGRP.
:LISTCOL VAR=JRNTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKJRN.Work with Journals - Help
:P.The journals the name selects. Option 2 applies journaled changes
to the files, option 3 takes them back out; options 5 and 8 show the
journal's receivers and the objects it covers.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
